# Frontend Rules (React + Vite)

## 1. Component structure
- Use functional components only
- Prefer named exports
- Keep components under 200 lines
- Extract reusable logic into hooks (useXxx)

## 2. State management
- Use useState/useReducer for local state
- Avoid unnecessary global state
- Use context only when truly needed

## 3. Hooks rules
- Do not call hooks conditionally
- Extract complex logic into custom hooks
- Keep hooks pure and reusable

## 4. Code style
- Use TypeScript strictly (no `any` unless necessary)
- Prefer early return instead of nested conditions
- Avoid duplicate logic

## 5. API calls
- Separate API layer in /services
- Never call fetch/axios directly inside components
- Handle loading/error states explicitly

## 6. File structure
- components/ → UI components
- pages/ → route-level components
- hooks/ → custom hooks
- services/ → API calls
- utils/ → helpers